  "problem": "It's known that there is a weak positive linear correlation between the variables $x$ and $y.$ Which of the following scatter plots corresponds to this situation?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's examine the given situation.\n\n- The *positive* linear correlation means that the data points should be scattered along a line with a *positive* slope.\n\n- Since the correlation is *weak*, most of the points should be scattered *far* from the trend line.\n\nTherefore, this situation corresponds to the following scatter plot.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14226558/assets/8c21367686723d7ce1165ec24f569658d77376a39d7962b8a4ed90b06c9e1220.png)",
